From dba79a1253921edf13e9be17ad1bd13886e91511 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yago Lasse <yagolasse@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:44:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] nv2a: pushbuffer frame capture + replay (RECOMP_PB_CAPTURE /
 _REPLAY)

Generic one-frame capture for the GPU renderer work: while RECOMP_PB_CAPTURE=<path> is set, every decoded method is mirrored into a last-value shadow table and one frame (RECOMP_PB_CAPTURE_FLIP=N) is recorded as a (subch, method, param) stream. At the flip the tool writes a self-contained file: the three guest-memory regions a draw reads (main RAM, the contiguous window, the NV2A aperture), the shadow replayed as ordinary commands plus the vertex program and constants re-uploaded as load + data, then the frame's own stream. No executor structs are snapshotted, so the same capture feeds any renderer (the software executor now, xemu's PGRAPH later).

RECOMP_PB_REPLAY=<path> restores the memory and the contiguous high-water mark (dma_resolve maps physical offsets against it), replays prelude + frame, and dumps a BMP. Replays byte-identically to the in-run reference for the first frame and the title screen.
